From 48113cfd28e12f0add6d8d20f2c17496eb4a7334 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:36:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(appium): accept driver package locations in useDrivers

A package that embeds Appium can now pass the location of a driver it
resolved with Node.js module resolution in `useDrivers`: an absolute path
or `file:` URL of the driver package, its package.json, or any file in it
(e.g. the result of `import.meta.resolve()` or `require.resolve()`).
Appium reads the driver metadata from that package instead of relying on
what is installed in APPIUM_HOME.

These drivers are kept in memory only, are never written to
extensions.yaml, and take precedence over installed drivers with the same
name or automationName.

Closes #19883
